{
  "slug": "armo-ctrl",
  "name": "Armo Ctrl",
  "type": "plugin",
  "description": "Drive the ARMO Cloud and Kubernetes security platform from natural language: incidents, CVEs, posture, runtime, and policies, with dry-run safety on every mutation.",
  "longDescription": "Ships **14 skills** and **1 hook**.\n\n- **Skills** (14): `armoctl` (ARMO security platform CLI — JSON-first agent-friendly access to runtime incidents, vulnerabilities, posture, risks, attack chains, inventory, network…), `armoctl-attack-chains` (Attack chains — multi-step kill-chain views built by ARMO from runtime + posture signal), `armoctl-cloud-accounts` (Cloud account onboarding — list/connect/disconnect ECS accounts), `armoctl-incidents` (ARMO runtime incidents — list active threats, fetch alerts on a single incident, explain an incident's signal, resolve/silence…), `armoctl-integrations` (Outbound integrations — alert channels (Slack/email/webhook), SIEM forwarders, Jira ticket creation), `armoctl-inventory` (Cluster inventory — list workloads, get unique values for a field), `armoctl-network-policies` (Generated NetworkPolicies — list discovered policies and generate one for a workload from observed traffic), `armoctl-posture` (Kubernetes posture scanning — controls, frameworks, exceptions), and 6 more\n- **Hooks** (1): `SessionStart`\n\nInstalls with `claude plugin install armo-ctrl@claude-community` from `armosec/armoctl`.",
  "compatibility": [
    "claude"
  ],
  "pluginType": "package",
  "package": {
    "skill": 14,
    "hook": 1
  },
  "sourceType": "community",
  "author": {
    "name": "ARMO",
    "url": "https://www.armosec.io"
  },
